osphorus and absence of treatment history", "Sarcoidosis: Could explain hypercalcemia but lacks supporting evidence in current findings"], "alarm_features": ["Unintentional weight loss", "Hypercalcemia (serum calcium >10.5 mg/dL)", "Multisystem involvement (respiratory, gastrointestinal, neurological symptoms)"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "PTH-mediated Hypercalcemia (Parathyroid Origin)", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.001, "danger": 0.6, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Malignancy-associated Hypercalcemia (PTHrP/Osteolytic Pathway)", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "reopened", "prior": 0.18011732967601068, "posterior": 0.20153401734026746, "danger": 0.9, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["The non-smoker status and absence of typical PTHrP-mediated malignancy features (e.g., anemia) provide weak against evidence for B2, though constitutional symp…"], "evidence_against": ["Absence of anemia and phosphorus elevation reduces malignancy-associated hypercalcemia (B2) plausibility, providing weak against evidence despite constitutiona…"], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.8, "interrupt_relevance": 0.9, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["primary hyperparathyroidism", "humoral hypercalcemia of malignancy", "milk-alkali syndrome", "sarcoidosis"]}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Vitamin-D / Granulomatous Hypercalcemia", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.0, "posterior": 0.5445121822041522, "danger": 0.5, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Normal phosphorus supports vitamin-D/granulomatous hypercalcemia (B3) over PTH-mediated mechanisms (B1), but since B1 is already closed, this provides modera